      "docTable": null,
      "label": "An order_by term after __name__",
      "status": "served",
      "driver": "node-sdk",
      "python": false,
      "note": "PR #85. Refused with INVALID_ARGUMENT and production's own message, measured against cloud-firestore-emulator v1.22.0 over raw gRPC. `served` rather than `unimplemented` on purpose: this is not a gap, it is the behaviour the row promises, and `unimplemented` would demand gRPC UNIMPLEMENTED plus fireup's own refusal wording — wrong for a refusal Firestore owns. The official Node SDK builds this shape unprompted from orderBy('__name__') plus an inequality filter, which is why serving it locally broke a real query in production."
